{
  "summary": "Reuses heap allocations in CoinsViewOverlay across blocks during parallel prevout fetching. It persists the intra-block transaction ID filter and worker task vector, avoids inserting the final transaction ID of a block into the filter, and relaxes ThreadPool::Submit to accept non-const lvalues while capping submitted tasks to the queued input count.",
  "problem": "CoinsViewOverlay::StartFetching reallocates and reseeds its earlier-txids hash set and allocates a task vector for every block connected. It also inserts the block's final transaction ID even though subsequent transactions cannot spend it, and dispatches worker threads that do no work when there are fewer queued inputs than workers.",
